 * Custom Budget-page tweaks for a self-hosted Actual Budget install.
 * GENERATED FILE — do not edit this file directly. It is built by
 * build-patch.js from actual-budget-tweaks.js.template + config.yml
 * (see config.example.yml). Every figure comes from the config; the
 * demo figures are placeholders, not real data. See README.md.
 * Loaded from build/index.html via:
 *   <script src="/actual-budget-tweaks.js"></script>
 *
 * What it does (Budget page only):
 *  1. Moves the Income group to the TOP of the budget table (it is
 *     rendered at the bottom by Actual).
 *  2. Shows income amounts in GREEN when they increase the balance.
 *  3. Shows the "Overspent in <month>" summary line in RED.
 *  4. Adds a COMPACT block above the budget table (no tall panel):
 *     - Savings-goal tracker at the top (quarterly + annual targets
 *       from the config), one slim progress bar per quarter.
 *     - Total net worth (incl. the home — value from the config) as one strip,
 *       plus the "back to the May amount?" line and a small detail
 *       line with the buckets. The down-payment placeholder is NOT
 *       counted alongside the home value — the home replaces it.
 *       Available funds is NOT shown anywhere. No standalone
 *       "Saved in the year" number. No month-by-month net-worth series.
 *     - "Spent in <month>" (validated live read from the Budget
 *       page header when readable, else demo figures). The reader
 *       validates the month, the budget and the spent amount before
 *       displaying anything live.
 *     - A compact monthly income-vs-spending bar strip (months from
 *       the config) with the saved amount under each month.
 *
 * What it does (Uncategorized transactions view only):
 *  5. Hides rows that are transfers (display only — no data is
 *     changed), so the list only shows transactions that genuinely
 *     need a category. A small note with a Show/Hide toggle is
 *     added above the table, and the view total is recomputed from
 *     the visible rows when it can be read reliably.
 *
 * v4 (config-driven): compact redesign — the tall v3 panel is gone
 * (the old panel element is removed if it is lingering). The Budget
 * page keeps its original compact feel and must keep scrolling.
 * Fixed the "Spent" bug (wrong month + wrong budget): the reader
 * now takes the month from the month selector / summary title and
 * the Budgeted/Spent totals from the table header, and validates
 * them (month must match the configured current month, budget within
 * $1 of the configured budget) before trusting them; otherwise it
 * falls back to the config figures.
 * The down-payment figure comes from the config.
 *
 * How it works: Actual is React, so a one-time DOM move would be undone
 * on the next render. This script therefore re-applies the tweaks with a
 * debounced MutationObserver. Every tweak is idempotent (it checks the
 * current state first), so the observer cannot loop.
 *
 * It is deliberately defensive: if Actual's DOM changes, each tweak
 * no-ops instead of throwing. Nothing here touches the budget data,
 * the server, or the API - it only reorders / restyles / adds a
 * compact block, and hides transfer rows in the Uncategorized view.
 *
 * The config figures are used as a FALLBACK. Whenever possible the net worth
 * reads the balances live from the sidebar account list, so it stays
 * current.
 */
